      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To push the modernization angle, argue that pre-colonial structures, while often complex, lacked the unified scale required for modern industrial economies or large-scale territorial administration. The colonial imposition of centralized governance and infrastructure acted as a powerful, albeit coercive, accelerator, forcibly integrating disparate local economies into national systems. Therefore, rather than viewing the colonial footprint as purely extractive, frame it as the necessary, brutal leap into the modern geopolitical and logistical reality that eventually allowed for autonomous state function.",
